{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Skein\/documentation\/Skein\/LifecycleAndErrors","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The global API owns one optional default application. List modules directly in its builder:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["try startSkein {","    appModule","    featureModule","}","defer { stopSkein() }","","let service: FeatureService = try get()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stopSkein()"},{"text":" detaches the application. Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await stopSkeinAndClose()"},{"text":" when cached values and active scopes must be disposed. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isSkeinStarted"},{"text":" is a snapshot; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"startSkeinIfNeeded"},{"text":" atomically installs only the first candidate and does not evaluate later builders.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Declared roots and validated startup","anchor":"Declared-roots-and-validated-startup","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Attach root policy to the binding that owns it. Structural roots validate constructor metadata without executing providers. Eager roots are structurally validated first, then resolved sequentially in declaration order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let featureModule = module {","    single(APIClient.self, using: APIClient.init)","    factory(FeatureService.self, using: FeatureService.init)","        .root(.eager)","}","","let application = try await SkeinApplication(validation: .declaredRoots) {","    featureModule","}","print(application.startupValidationReport?.opaqueBindings ?? [])"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Validated global startup is also async and publishes nothing after a validation failure:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let installed = try await startSkeinIfNeeded(validation: .declaredRoots) {","    appModule","    featureModule","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"After global publication, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"currentSkeinValidationReport"},{"text":" exposes the installed application’s report under the lifecycle lock and returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" after stop.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Opaque closure providers appear in the validation report but are not failures. Constructor registrations expose all parameter-pack edges. Scoped roots and eager assisted roots are rejected; structural assisted roots are allowed.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Errors and diagnostics","anchor":"Errors-and-diagnostics","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Lifecycle failures are direct ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkeinError"},{"text":" values. Resolution failures are ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkeinResolutionError"},{"text":", which contains the underlying error and source-aware path frames. Invalid compositions fail with typed configuration errors. Isolation mismatches identify the required and actual binding isolation.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Provider side effects are not rolled back if a later eager root fails. Eager singles remain cached; eager factories run during startup and again on later resolution.","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Lifecycle, validation, and errors","modules":[{"name":"Skein"}]},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"Documentation index","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Skein\/documentation\/Skein","type":"reference","overridi